{{feat
|type=general
|prereq=proficiency with the chosen weapon, [[base attack bonus]] +8
|reqfor=[[overwhelming critical]], [[devastating critical]]
|desc=Combat ability increases the critical [[threat range]] of a selected weapon by a range equal to the item's base threat range. A [[longsword]] that normally threatens a critical on a roll of 19-20 would now threaten a critical on a roll of 17-20.
|use=automatic. The threat range of a [[keen]] weapon is already doubled, increasing to triple with this feat. This feat can be selected multiple times, applying to a new weapon category each time.
|special=[[Halfling]]s and [[gnome]]s are small creatures, and as such they can never use the following large weapons: dire mace, double-bladed sword, doubleaxe, greataxe, greatsword, halberd, heavy flail, and scythe.
|bonus1=champion of Torm
|bonus2=fighter
}}

== Notes ==

* [[Paladin]]s can choose ''improved critical'' in the [[whip]] as an [[epic bonus feat]]. This is likely a bug as they cannot select this feat for any other weapon as a bonus feat.
* The [[creature weapon]] variant of this feat is non-functional; the [[unarmed strike]] variant is used with creature weapons (or any other [[natural weapon]]).
* There is no variant of this feat for the [[magic staff]].

==Builder notes==

'''Item feat:''' Only ''improved critical (unarmed)''; the rest can be added with custom content.

==Custom content notes==

'''Removable:''' yes

'''Reusable:''' yes

'''Script:''' hardcoded

*These [[feat]]s can be added to [[iprp_feats.2da]] to make them available as item feats.
*New ''improved critical'' feats for new weapon types cannot be created, but existing weapon types can be overwritten.